{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Whimsical Play.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Whimsical Play.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"whimsical play whimsical play","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Whimsical Play.md","fileName":"Whimsical Play.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Whimsical Play","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 00:27\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Play Styles and Structures]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Play Styles and Structures","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Whimsical Play.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Whimsical Play.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"whimsical play whimsical play","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Whimsical Play.md","fileName":"Whimsical Play.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Whimsical Play","heading":"Whimsical Play","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Whimsical play creates pleasure through silly actions, surprising consequences, bodily exuberance, or conceptual absurdity. Its rules often make an ordinary behavior strange enough that the sensation of performing it becomes the main event.\n\nWhimsy can arise from constraint as readily as freedom. An awkward controller, deliberately unstable movement, or an implausible rule can produce a coherent experience when the resulting unpredictability supports the game's comic or euphoric character.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Play Styles and Structures","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Whimsical Play.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Whimsical Play.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"whimsical play whimsical play","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Whimsical Play.md","fileName":"Whimsical Play.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Whimsical Play","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[gamesdesignandplay.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Play Styles and Structures","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}